From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:42:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/43] perf(dsl): stream msgpack-compact ACIR program and
 witness decoding

circuit_buf_to_acir_format unpacked the whole program (including the Brillig functions and the
assert messages, ~1/3 of the bytes) into one msgpack object tree, converted it into a full
Acir::Circuit, and only then into AcirFormat. For the msgpack-compact array layout it now walks
the outer arrays by hand, unpacks one opcode at a time into a reused zone (STR/BIN referencing the
input buffer) and feeds it straight to an incremental AcirFormatConverter; the Brillig functions,
function name, private parameters and assert messages are skipped. circuit_serde_to_acir_format
uses the same converter, so both paths produce the same AcirFormat.

witness_buf_to_witness_vector reads the compact witness map directly into the WitnessVector
(no object tree, no std::map of byte vectors). The map is validated in full (uint32 keys in strictly
increasing order, 32-byte bin8 values) before any value is written, and holes are filled with
random elements in the same order as witness_map_to_witness_vector.

Any other layout falls back to the generic decoders.
